1
00:01:40,625 --> 00:01:41,465
He!

2
00:01:51,145 --> 00:01:52,265
He!

3
00:01:52,785 --> 00:01:53,905
He!

4
00:02:00,185 --> 00:02:01,265
<i>He!</i>

5
00:02:05,145 --> 00:02:06,305
<i>He!</i>

6
00:02:06,985 --> 00:02:10,744
In 2002, my dad
had a stroke for the first time,

7
00:02:11,625 --> 00:02:13,425
and he fell into the rooftop shaft.

8
00:02:14,105 --> 00:02:15,065
And then,

9
00:02:16,025 --> 00:02:18,825
he was heavily injured in an operation.

10
00:02:20,385 --> 00:02:21,625
And later,

11
00:02:22,945 --> 00:02:27,265
the sudden passing of his apprentice
exacerbated his condition.

12
00:02:27,345 --> 00:02:28,985
Two years ago, he went into retirement.

13
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:30,865
Out of nowhere, he received
something left behind by his apprentice.

14
00:02:31,545 --> 00:02:33,105
Perhaps it triggered something in him.

15
00:02:33,185 --> 00:02:35,945
His condition acted up, and he fainted.

16
00:02:36,585 --> 00:02:38,545
In his mind, his apprentice never died.

17
00:02:38,625 --> 00:02:41,305
He merely went to Beijing
to teach for 12 years.

18
00:02:41,825 --> 00:02:43,825
Whenever his apprentice appeared,

19
00:02:43,905 --> 00:02:46,745
he'd convince him to stay
to help him investigate cases.

20
00:02:47,465 --> 00:02:51,105
It seems like his memory is stuck in 2002.

21
00:03:18,105 --> 00:03:19,865
I waited for you for five years!

22
00:03:20,945 --> 00:03:22,105
Why didn't you save me?

23
00:03:22,185 --> 00:03:23,465
Why?

24
00:03:24,265 --> 00:03:25,665
Come back.

25
00:03:26,265 --> 00:03:28,225
I'm waiting for you. Come down.

26
00:03:28,305 --> 00:03:30,705
Keep me company. You…

27
00:04:02,225 --> 00:04:03,265
Doctor.

28
00:04:03,345 --> 00:04:04,785
Doctor!

29
00:04:06,385 --> 00:04:08,225
He. You're awake.

30
00:04:08,825 --> 00:04:10,265
Why am I here?

31
00:04:14,905 --> 00:04:16,944
You fell into the rooftop shaft yesterday.

32
00:04:17,025 --> 00:04:19,624
Fortunately, no bone fractures.
Just some cuts.

33
00:04:19,705 --> 00:04:20,905
Fortunately?

34
00:04:20,985 --> 00:04:22,184
Officer He,

35
00:04:22,265 --> 00:04:25,185
you fell because you had a stroke,
and you lost consciousness.

36
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,345
I checked your medical records.

37
00:04:26,425 --> 00:04:28,145
Your cholesterol, blood sugar,
and blood pressure levels

38
00:04:28,225 --> 00:04:29,345
are dangerously high.

39
00:04:29,425 --> 00:04:30,785
Did you take medication regularly?

40
00:04:31,385 --> 00:04:33,905
Taking pills during all three of my meals?

41
00:04:33,985 --> 00:04:35,225
Who can live like that?

42
00:04:35,305 --> 00:04:36,225
Listen.

43
00:04:36,305 --> 00:04:38,465
Your condition is serious.
You have to take your medication.

44
00:04:38,545 --> 00:04:40,705
Otherwise, this will happen again,

45
00:04:40,785 --> 00:04:42,785
-and it will be more serious.
-Okay.

46
00:04:43,745 --> 00:04:45,145
There are no other huge issues,

47
00:04:45,225 --> 00:04:46,985
but you will stay here for a few days.

48
00:04:47,065 --> 00:04:48,265
Thanks, Doctor.

49
00:05:02,665 --> 00:05:03,505
Captain Feng just left.

50
00:05:04,825 --> 00:05:06,105
He told me everything.

51
00:05:07,345 --> 00:05:10,825
Are you intending
to take full responsibility?

52
00:05:11,945 --> 00:05:14,945
Did you tell Captain Feng
that you want to go to Beijing to teach?

53
00:05:25,625 --> 00:05:26,545
He.

54
00:05:29,625 --> 00:05:32,705
I'd like to apologize to you.
It's my fault.

55
00:05:33,385 --> 00:05:36,185
Whether it's the missing persons case
or the homicide,

56
00:05:36,265 --> 00:05:39,705
I shouldn't have brought
my emotions into the case.

57
00:05:48,825 --> 00:05:49,865
Give me your hand.

58
00:05:51,105 --> 00:05:53,105
-That hand.
-Why?

59
00:05:54,065 --> 00:05:54,905
Press this.

60
00:05:57,625 --> 00:05:59,185
He, what are you doing?
What about your IV drip?

61
00:05:59,265 --> 00:06:01,145
Now is not the time to lie down.

62
00:06:01,905 --> 00:06:03,025
Let's go. We have a case to crack.

63
00:06:06,425 --> 00:06:07,265
Come.

64
00:06:13,945 --> 00:06:14,825
In the June 30th case,

65
00:06:14,905 --> 00:06:17,625
Song Qingsong is undeniably
the main suspect.

66
00:06:17,705 --> 00:06:21,305
But he allegedly fled
to the US five years ago.

67
00:06:22,545 --> 00:06:23,945
Immigrating is suspicious enough.

68
00:06:24,025 --> 00:06:26,305
Back then, Song Qingsong
hired someone to commit a murder.

69
00:06:26,385 --> 00:06:29,225
But he was acquitted
due to a lack of evidence.

70
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:31,225
We could only charge him with bribery.

71
00:06:31,305 --> 00:06:33,065
Even then, it wasn't that serious.

72
00:06:33,145 --> 00:06:35,025
He would get five years in jail at most.

73
00:06:35,105 --> 00:06:37,185
And when he would be released,
he would still be the same old him.

74
00:06:37,265 --> 00:06:40,185
The factory, the car,
and the property would still be his.

75
00:06:40,785 --> 00:06:41,785
So why did he flee?

76
00:06:41,865 --> 00:06:43,585
I did investigate him.

77
00:06:43,665 --> 00:06:45,625
Song Qingsong had dealings in both
legitimate and illegitimate channels.

78
00:06:45,705 --> 00:06:47,785
He's definitely not a good person,

79
00:06:47,865 --> 00:06:49,705
but he's kind to his factory workers.

80
00:06:49,785 --> 00:06:51,465
Those workers have worked
for him for more than a decade.

81
00:06:51,545 --> 00:06:55,105
Oh. He also has a son
who was only three years old when he fled.

82
00:06:56,265 --> 00:07:00,465
So there's probably another story
behind his hiring of the hitman.

83
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:02,585
The most effective way

84
00:07:02,665 --> 00:07:04,825
to investigate Song Qingsong
is through Wu Shanlong.

85
00:07:04,905 --> 00:07:07,745
But after he took over the cement factory,
he accrued debts

86
00:07:07,825 --> 00:07:09,225
and is now in hiding.

87
00:07:10,745 --> 00:07:11,985
Turn right at the intersection in front.

88
00:07:13,225 --> 00:07:14,265
We're not returning to the station?

89
00:07:14,345 --> 00:07:16,105
Shouldn't we find Wu Shanlong?

90
00:07:22,985 --> 00:07:26,025
HONGYUN HUIHUANG CLUB

91
00:07:39,505 --> 00:07:40,625
Who are you?

92
00:07:40,705 --> 00:07:42,425
This is the dressing room.

93
00:07:45,225 --> 00:07:48,025
Are you new here?

94
00:07:50,625 --> 00:07:52,705
I'm Wu. W-U.

95
00:07:53,425 --> 00:07:54,745
Shanlong is my name.

96
00:07:55,345 --> 00:07:58,865
I am the biggest shareholder of this club.

97
00:07:58,945 --> 00:08:01,025
Qingsong Cement Factory. Ever heard of it?

98
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:02,385
It's mine too.

99
00:08:04,425 --> 00:08:07,225
Perhaps I could book all of you today,

100
00:08:07,945 --> 00:08:10,945
so that you can get some good rest.

101
00:08:12,105 --> 00:08:13,145
Hi, Mei.

102
00:08:13,825 --> 00:08:15,185
-Hi, Mei.
-Hi, Mei.

103
00:08:15,265 --> 00:08:16,825
Hi.

104
00:08:21,265 --> 00:08:22,625
Come out here.

105
00:08:38,664 --> 00:08:40,825
Leeching off this place every day.

106
00:08:42,345 --> 00:08:44,105
Do I owe you anything or what?

107
00:08:49,305 --> 00:08:51,105
Did I hear that correctly?

108
00:08:51,185 --> 00:08:53,385
Do you even know who you're talking to?

109
00:08:54,145 --> 00:08:55,145
Wu Shanlong.

110
00:08:55,825 --> 00:08:57,465
From now on,

111
00:08:57,545 --> 00:08:59,625
I won't lend a single cent to you.

112
00:09:02,865 --> 00:09:05,385
Zhao Hongmei. I see you've grown arrogant.

113
00:09:05,465 --> 00:09:06,865
Without me,

114
00:09:06,945 --> 00:09:09,025
you would still have been the owner
of that small massage parlor.

115
00:09:09,105 --> 00:09:10,705
Who gave you your first fortune?

116
00:09:10,785 --> 00:09:12,345
It was me, Wu Shanlong. It was me.

117
00:09:12,425 --> 00:09:14,385
Without me, this place would still
be called Dahuihuang.

118
00:09:18,865 --> 00:09:20,105
You helped me?

119
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:21,785
Do you even have the wits for it?

120
00:09:21,865 --> 00:09:23,225
Without me,

121
00:09:23,305 --> 00:09:25,185
Song Qingsong would still
be running the cement factory,

122
00:09:25,705 --> 00:09:28,225
-and you would still be his chauffeur.
-What did you say?

123
00:09:28,305 --> 00:09:30,265
-I gave you your share of the money.
-Say that again.

124
00:09:30,345 --> 00:09:32,585
I gave you your share of the money.
You are just incompetent.

125
00:09:32,665 --> 00:09:35,225
The cement factory was a gold mine,
but you messed it up.

126
00:09:36,025 --> 00:09:38,585
And now, you're leeching off me.

127
00:09:38,665 --> 00:09:41,345
I've treated you with enough generosity.

128
00:09:42,065 --> 00:09:43,425
Am I the shareholder here or not?

129
00:09:43,505 --> 00:09:45,345
I can come and go whenever I want.

130
00:09:45,425 --> 00:09:48,065
Of course. Come whenever you want.

131
00:09:49,185 --> 00:09:51,025
But before you come,

132
00:09:51,545 --> 00:09:53,785
clean up the mess you made.

133
00:09:53,865 --> 00:09:55,305
What mess?

134
00:09:55,385 --> 00:09:57,105
Tell me. What mess?

135
00:09:57,185 --> 00:09:58,745
Still playing dumb?

136
00:09:59,665 --> 00:10:01,145
The police just released a statement.

137
00:10:01,225 --> 00:10:04,065
Xu Zhihong's body was found in Yuanlongli.

138
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:05,705
They are investigating it everywhere now.

139
00:10:09,665 --> 00:10:10,905
You killed Xu Meng too.

140
00:10:11,585 --> 00:10:14,225
You are now a murderer.

141
00:10:14,305 --> 00:10:16,025
Why don't you learn
from your brother-in-law?

142
00:10:16,105 --> 00:10:18,945
Just run away. Run.

143
00:10:19,025 --> 00:10:21,665
When you're gone, everyone will be safe.

144
00:10:22,345 --> 00:10:24,105
The girls under me?

145
00:10:24,945 --> 00:10:27,745
I can't guarantee
they are as loyal as I am.

146
00:10:27,825 --> 00:10:29,705
If one of them gets drunk
and runs their mouth,

147
00:10:29,785 --> 00:10:31,105
I won't be able to stop them.

148
00:10:32,065 --> 00:10:32,905
Sure.

149
00:10:35,105 --> 00:10:36,065
I can run away.

150
00:10:36,145 --> 00:10:38,225
But I need you to give me some money.

151
00:10:38,305 --> 00:10:39,865
Are you crazy?

152
00:10:51,265 --> 00:10:52,105
Zhao Hongmei.

153
00:10:54,025 --> 00:10:56,225
You're talking to a murderer now.

154
00:10:57,385 --> 00:10:59,905
How many lives do you risk by defying me?

155
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:06,785
Defying you? What about that?

156
00:11:06,865 --> 00:11:09,025
What about that?
I won't comply, so kill me now.

157
00:11:10,745 --> 00:11:13,025
Do you want to see
if I will go to the police right now?

158
00:11:13,105 --> 00:11:14,545
Please be patient, sir.

159
00:11:14,625 --> 00:11:16,225
Our manager is having a meeting. You…

160
00:11:21,065 --> 00:11:23,345
What a coincidence.
My two old friends are here.

161
00:11:23,425 --> 00:11:25,265
Great. Let's hang out.

162
00:11:27,225 --> 00:11:29,585
Officer He. Officer Ran. You're here.

163
00:11:29,665 --> 00:11:32,865
I was just reminiscing
about the past with Mr. Wu here.

164
00:11:32,945 --> 00:11:34,025
We talked about you two.

165
00:11:34,105 --> 00:11:36,985
-Speak of the devil, really.
-Is that so?

166
00:11:38,025 --> 00:11:39,145
-Zhang!
-Yes?

167
00:11:39,225 --> 00:11:41,025
How is the speaker outside going?

168
00:11:41,105 --> 00:11:43,425
-It's almost done, Mei.
-Show me.

169
00:11:44,105 --> 00:11:46,465
I have work to do. Mr. Hu,

170
00:11:46,545 --> 00:11:49,025
entertain our old friends here, will you?

171
00:11:49,105 --> 00:11:50,145
I'll count on you. Take a seat.

172
00:11:50,225 --> 00:11:51,905
Order anything you want. Take a seat.

173
00:11:52,665 --> 00:11:53,905
Take a seat.

174
00:11:53,985 --> 00:11:54,945
Officer Ran!

175
00:11:55,545 --> 00:11:56,945
You're more handsome than before.

176
00:12:10,985 --> 00:12:12,105
Speak.

177
00:12:12,185 --> 00:12:14,465
Tell us about Xu Meng and her father.

178
00:12:16,145 --> 00:12:17,825
What are you on about, Officer He?

179
00:12:18,505 --> 00:12:19,585
I don't know them.

180
00:12:23,225 --> 00:12:24,745
Wu Shanlong,

181
00:12:24,825 --> 00:12:27,385
between us, there's no need to play coy.

182
00:12:31,745 --> 00:12:34,465
Back then, Song Qingsong hired a hitman
to kill Xu Meng and her father.

183
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:36,345
You did it, didn't you?

184
00:12:41,305 --> 00:12:42,585
How did Xu Zhihong die?

185
00:12:42,665 --> 00:12:45,385
Where is Xu Meng? Is she dead or alive?

186
00:12:50,385 --> 00:12:51,505
Speak!

187
00:12:57,025 --> 00:12:59,065
I'll speak. Officer He,
I'll tell you everything.

188
00:12:59,145 --> 00:13:00,225
I'll come clean.

189
00:13:00,305 --> 00:13:02,505
I'll tell you everything.

190
00:13:03,465 --> 00:13:05,065
Song Qingsong gave me 40,000 yuan

191
00:13:05,145 --> 00:13:06,745
to get rid of Xu Meng and her father.

192
00:13:06,825 --> 00:13:08,745
He doesn't care about laws, but I do.

193
00:13:09,905 --> 00:13:11,545
I paid you to get rid of them,

194
00:13:11,625 --> 00:13:12,665
and what did you do?

195
00:13:12,745 --> 00:13:14,025
I asked you to do it yourself,

196
00:13:14,105 --> 00:13:15,505
but you paid someone else
to do it instead.

197
00:13:15,585 --> 00:13:17,905
That deal could have cost me my life.

198
00:13:17,985 --> 00:13:20,825
I wouldn't have done it,
even if he had punched me to death.

199
00:13:20,905 --> 00:13:22,025
What about Wolfie?

200
00:13:23,585 --> 00:13:25,665
You know him very well, don't you?

201
00:13:27,425 --> 00:13:28,785
Get rid of them.

202
00:13:33,625 --> 00:13:36,105
What? What wolf?

203
00:13:36,705 --> 00:13:38,105
I don't know him.

204
00:13:38,865 --> 00:13:39,705
Sure.

205
00:13:39,785 --> 00:13:41,745
You said it had nothing to do with you.

206
00:13:41,825 --> 00:13:43,105
Then tell me.

207
00:13:43,185 --> 00:13:44,945
How did Xu Zhihong die?

208
00:13:48,785 --> 00:13:51,385
Based on my understanding
of Song Qingsong,

209
00:13:51,465 --> 00:13:53,385
he must have hired someone else to do it.

210
00:13:53,465 --> 00:13:55,705
Achieve his goals at all costs.

211
00:13:55,785 --> 00:13:56,985
That's his personality.

212
00:13:57,065 --> 00:14:00,225
Why must Song Qingsong
get rid of Xu Meng and her father?

213
00:14:00,305 --> 00:14:01,545
I know why.

214
00:14:02,145 --> 00:14:03,025
Back then, Xu Meng

215
00:14:03,105 --> 00:14:04,945
saw the tender document
inside Song Qingsong's briefcase

216
00:14:05,025 --> 00:14:05,945
in the foot massage parlor.

217
00:14:06,025 --> 00:14:08,705
Then, she wrote to Song Qingsong
to extort money.

218
00:14:08,785 --> 00:14:10,385
Song Qingsong was furious

219
00:14:10,465 --> 00:14:12,025
and wanted her gone.

220
00:14:12,105 --> 00:14:14,145
Getting rid of her father
was just an afterthought.

221
00:14:14,225 --> 00:14:16,025
Why didn't you tell us back then?

222
00:14:17,145 --> 00:14:19,185
Because he was my brother-in-law.

223
00:14:19,265 --> 00:14:20,665
But now, it's different.

224
00:14:20,745 --> 00:14:22,785
Just ask me whatever you want to know.

225
00:14:22,865 --> 00:14:24,545
I'll tell you everything I know.

226
00:14:36,585 --> 00:14:37,585
Wu Shanlong.

227
00:14:37,665 --> 00:14:41,425
Have you contacted
Song Qingsong in recent years?

228
00:14:43,905 --> 00:14:45,945
We lost contact five years ago.

229
00:14:46,025 --> 00:14:48,865
I don't know where he's hiding now.

230
00:14:52,025 --> 00:14:53,065
Sir,

231
00:14:53,585 --> 00:14:55,385
if he contacts me,

232
00:14:56,625 --> 00:14:59,945
I promise to contact
the police right away.

233
00:15:43,705 --> 00:15:46,465
Wu Shanlong. Do not leave Weiyang.

234
00:15:46,545 --> 00:15:47,985
We will talk to you anytime.

235
00:15:49,705 --> 00:15:51,865
Sure, sir. I won't leave.

236
00:15:53,185 --> 00:15:54,825
Drop by when you're free.

237
00:16:06,305 --> 00:16:10,025
HONGYUN HUIHUANG CLUB

238
00:16:22,345 --> 00:16:24,265
That liar.

239
00:16:24,865 --> 00:16:26,265
Not a word of truth from his mouth.

240
00:16:26,345 --> 00:16:28,225
I made sure to ask him about Wolfie,

241
00:16:28,305 --> 00:16:29,905
and his eyes looked to the right.

242
00:16:31,625 --> 00:16:33,505
He knows that we don't have evidence,

243
00:16:34,105 --> 00:16:35,065
and we can't do anything about him.

244
00:16:38,345 --> 00:16:40,545
Now that the lead
on Song Qingsong is stuck,

245
00:16:40,625 --> 00:16:43,345
we can only find
another breakthrough in the scene.

246
00:16:47,225 --> 00:16:48,305
He.

247
00:16:48,385 --> 00:16:50,825
I want to go through
the suspicious residents

248
00:16:50,905 --> 00:16:51,745
in Yuanlongli again.

249
00:16:53,025 --> 00:16:54,505
You still want to head to Yuanlongli?

250
00:16:55,385 --> 00:16:56,905
What if you're stuck in there?

251
00:17:02,425 --> 00:17:03,265
He.

252
00:17:03,785 --> 00:17:05,385
Have you heard
of the Eye of the Vortex Theory?

253
00:17:06,105 --> 00:17:06,944
What?

254
00:17:07,025 --> 00:17:10,025
The eye of the vortex
is the center of the vortex.

255
00:17:10,105 --> 00:17:11,305
To see it,

256
00:17:11,385 --> 00:17:13,345
you must venture into the vortex.

257
00:17:13,985 --> 00:17:15,704
New York Block
is at the center of the crime,

258
00:17:15,785 --> 00:17:16,905
the eye of the vortex.

259
00:17:16,985 --> 00:17:18,985
Residents might come and go,

260
00:17:19,065 --> 00:17:21,545
but as long as the building's there,
we will find useful leads.

261
00:17:29,145 --> 00:17:30,145
What?

262
00:17:30,225 --> 00:17:32,065
You almost had it there.

263
00:17:32,145 --> 00:17:33,945
I thought you had lost your mind.

264
